  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates the most favorable outcome with the minimum probability in each lottery and prefers the one with the more favorable (higher) such outcome. In this case, Lottery B has the higher amount (2500) with a slightly lower probability (33%), making it the preferred option under the reason. The individual also bases their choice on the higher euro amount in Lottery B, explicitly citing the larger potential win as the justification. Although the individual does not explicitly reference probabilities or label the outcome as 'least probable,' the reasoning aligns with focusing on the best possible outcome and preferring the lottery with the higher such outcome. Given that the best outcome in each lottery is also the least probable one (since both lotteries have only one positive outcome), the information considered by the individual matches the information required by the decision reason. The justification, while not technically precise, reflects the same preference rule: choose the lottery with the more favorable (higher) least probable outcome. Therefore, the individual’s reasoning is consistent with the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
